{"id": "EUVD-2026-103833", "enisaUuid": "737b11cf-c6a3-3f8a-b015-21653631d62e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nserial: 8250_bcm7271: fix use-after-free in brcmuart_remove()\n\nbrcmuart_handle_irq() starts priv->hrt to work around a receive-timeout\nquirk of the 8250 core when hardware flow control is enabled; the timer\ncallback brcmuart_hrtimer_func() dereferences priv.\n\nbrcmuart_remove() cancels the hrtimer before it unregisters the port, so\na receive-timeout interrupt that arrives in between re-arms the timer.\nAfter devm frees priv, the callback runs on freed memory.\n\nUnregister the port before cancelling the hrtimer.\nserial8250_unregister_port() shuts the port down and frees its IRQ, so\nbrcmuart_handle_irq() can no longer restart the timer, and the final\nhrtimer_cancel() drains any timer that was armed before or during the\nunregister.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd81650bec58ac70e5dfde2ec390acc1f0d1ed76", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5ce06e648d775cc1ccf66f4f594bb8b559a7d8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e32440fa536af96bdbc61d933a7c3a920b965edc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0794ba5332754866b2f1c0cca668775be3ffcf0a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/189b9dc8c96ec9486482f27c1372b04a7152175e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98748", "GHSA-7g75-q55x-6r4j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20220172-e10f-3b80-b9ea-064f67073bb8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "2812ee11-e1ad-3645-b279-317a57308b7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "2978f01a-5140-33cd-b3df-b4a7ab7287a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "41a4694